---
import GovernanceLayout from '../../layouts/GovernanceLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../data/site';
---

<GovernanceLayout
  title="Corrections"
  description="Commercial Roofing Intel's corrections policy: how to report an error, how quickly we act, and how corrections are disclosed."
  crumbName="Corrections"
  lede="An authority that hides its mistakes isn't one. Here is exactly what happens when CRI gets something wrong."
  updated="2026-07-15"
>
  <h2>Report an error</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a> with the page URL
    and the issue, or use the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>. Anyone may report an
    error — readers, contractors, manufacturers, competitors. The source of the report
    never affects how it is handled.
  </p>

  <h2>What happens next</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Acknowledgment.</strong> We confirm receipt as promptly as we can, and correction reports are prioritised over other correspondence.</li>
    <li><strong>Verification.</strong> The claim is checked against sources under our <a href="/about/editorial-standards/">Editorial Standards</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Correction.</strong> Verified factual errors are corrected as soon as verification completes. We would rather be right than fast, but we do not sit on confirmed errors.</li>
    <li><strong>Disclosure.</strong> Material corrections are noted on the corrected page with the date and nature of the change.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>What counts as material</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Errors that could change a reader’s decision (costs, service life, code requirements, warranty conditions, safety guidance) are always material and always disclosed.</li>
    <li>Typos and formatting fixes that do not change meaning are corrected silently.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Disagreements that aren’t errors</h2>
  <p>
    Sometimes qualified people disagree with our conclusions without a factual error being
    involved. Where a substantive methodological objection has merit, we update the page or
    add the competing view with its evidence — see <a href="/about/methodology/">Methodology</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Correction log</h2>
  <div class="callout">
    <strong class="callout__title">No corrections issued yet</strong>
    Material corrections will be listed here with dates and affected pages once the site is live.
  </div>
</GovernanceLayout>
